# Vocabulary versions implemented in this repo.
# Compare against spec/VOCAB_VERSIONS to detect drift.
# Run scripts/check-downstream-versions.sh from spec/ to check all repos at once.
# Update this file when the system prompt or agent capabilities reflect new vocabulary.
# core 3.3 (2026-06-16): added cascade:AIAsserted (ungrounded general-purpose-AI
#   provenance leaf), cascade:ProxyAgent (caregiver-proxy actor + actsForPatient/
#   proxyRelationship/proxyGrantedAt/etc.); plus cascade:AIGenerationActivity,
#   cascade:AdvisoryApplicationActivity, cascade:GenerationTrigger (from v3.1/3.2).
# clinical 1.9 (2026-06-17): shapes-only — cascade:AIExtracted is now a valid
#   cascade:dataProvenance value on clinical records.
# 2026-07-15 batched draft sync: taught the system prompt the notes/ oa:Annotation
#   container (workbench v1-draft.0.5), the evidence facet model (evidence v1-draft.0.2),
#   and workbench:userSourceLabel (v1-draft.0.4). Per D-PATH, drafts stay unrowed until
#   v1.0 graduation; no version row change.
# core 3.4 (2026-08-03): the pod export manifest is now describable vocabulary, so the
#   prompt teaches reading manifest.ttl as a first orienting call instead of only parsing
#   it: cascade:ExportManifest (a dcat:Dataset), cascade:RecordSummary (a void:Dataset
#   whose per-domain counts are rdfs:subPropertyOf void:entities) and the seven count
#   properties, cascade:InteractionScenario (+ involvedResources / severity /
#   requiresCrossProvenance), and cascade:provenanceLayers. Also teaches that the five
#   *Days properties count DAYS COVERED and must never be reported as record counts, and
#   adds the reading-level terms cascade:date (with the health:date second spelling),
#   cascade:sampleCount and cascade:loincCode.
# health 2.5 (2026-08-03): the five clinical record classes (health:LabResultRecord,
#   ConditionRecord, AllergyRecord, ImmunizationRecord, FamilyHistoryRecord) are now
#   defined and shaped, and the six wellness containers (health:ActivityData, SleepData,
#   HeartRateData, BloodPressureData, HRVData, BodyMeasurements) are rdfs:subClassOf
#   health:HealthProfile, so the prompt now says the history properties hang off those six
#   subjects. Also teaches the namespace-boundary rule: health: vs clinical: is historical,
#   not a provenance signal — cascade:dataProvenance is the only source-of-truth for origin.
# clinical 1.13 (2026-08-03): clinical:LabResult / Condition / Allergy / Immunization are
#   deprecated in favour of their health: equivalents but are NOT removed, no emitter
#   changed, and existing pods hold both. The prompt gains a dedicated "Two Spellings"
#   section teaching that both must be queried, with the per-concept predicate table (the
#   two spellings share no predicates), and every clinical jq example in the prompt now
#   reads both. Also teaches the v1.10-v1.12 graph edges clinical:hasEncounter,
#   clinical:indicationReference (traverse the superproperty to get both stated and
#   clinical:parsedIndicationReference edges, and present them differently) and
#   clinical:linkedCondition superseding the untraversable clinical:linkedConditionIds
#   literal, plus the new ConsultationNote shape and the two unenforced value sets.
# health 2.6 / clinical 1.14 / coverage 1.4 / checkup 3.3 (2026-08-08): shapes-only
#   alignment to ratified standards (spec PR the-cascade-protocol/spec#16). The system
#   prompt is taught the four facts that change what the agent may ASSUME when reading a
#   pod: lab interpretation is the HL7 v3 ObservationInterpretation code system (and
#   "unknown" means the source carried none, not "normal"); labCategory, testCode,
#   icd10Code and snomedCode are repeatable, so a dual-coded problem is one condition and
#   not two; source-carried dates may be xsd:date, and a date with no time means the time
#   was not recorded; clinical:Encounter is now validated at all, and coverage:coverageType
#   is no longer a closed enum. checkup 3.3 is an ICD-10-CM pattern fix with no agent-facing
#   consequence and is recorded here only to keep the rows in step.
# core 3.5 (2026-08-15): cascade:sourceIdentity, the ORIGIN axis. The prompt now teaches the
#   three source axes as three different questions and says which one may be keyed on: ORIGIN
#   (cascade:sourceIdentity, a canonical transport-independent organization token, the only
#   reconciliation and grouping key), LABEL (clinical:sourceEHR, display only) and INGESTION
#   (cascade:sourceSystem, the import batch, explicitly never an origin). The scheme prefix is
#   taught as load-bearing: org: is a derived organization, ns: is only an assigning authority,
#   and transport: means origin unknown and must never be read as a shared source. The
#   "records from one organization" query pattern groups on sourceIdentity, not sourceSystem.
# core 3.6 (2026-08-15): cascade:dataAbsentReason, bound to the 15 FHIR data-absent-reason
#   codes. The prompt teaches that a record carrying it has NO value, that the reason is an
#   ANSWER and must never be reported as "no data" or an empty result, that asked-declined /
#   not-asked / asked-unknown / temp-unknown are four different clinical facts, that the
#   property explains the absence of the record's VALUE only, and that a raw HL7 v3 NullFlavor
#   code in the property is an importer defect rather than a code to interpret (the mapping
#   table is included so the agent can say what should have been written).
# health 2.7 / clinical 1.15 (2026-08-15): health:interpretationSourceCode and
#   clinical:interpretationSourceCode, the verbatim escape hatch for a source interpretation
#   code that is in neither bound value set. The prompt teaches reading it ALONGSIDE the
#   normalized interpretation so the source's own word stays quotable (interpretation "A" plus
#   interpretationSourceCode "elevated"), quoting the source code and computing on the
#   normalized one. The interpretation value set moves from 60 to 74 values (49 selectable HL7
#   v3 ObservationInterpretation codes, all 15 data-absent-reason codes, 10 retained legacy
#   words), so the v1.14 note that "unknown" is the only absence code is retired. Vital-sign
#   clinical:interpretation is now bound to the same set at warning severity, which expires the
#   v1.13 note that it is unconstrained. clinical 1.15 also opens the PROCEDURE NAME migration
#   window: clinical:procedureName is canonical and the only spelling a producer may write, but
#   a C-CDA import path wrote health:procedureName on records typed clinical:Procedure, so the
#   prompt teaches reading BOTH predicates (canonical first) and adds a procedures query
#   pattern. Procedure was also missing from the supported-data-types list and is now listed.
# core 3.7 / health 2.8 / clinical 1.16 / coverage 1.5 (2026-08-27, wave 4): the release
#   that made a visit answerable. clinical:hasParticipant -> clinical:EncounterParticipant
#   (participantName / participantRole / participantRoleCode / participantSpecialty) replaces
#   "read clinical:providerName and hope": providerName is RETAINED as the single display
#   name, so the prompt now says every who-was-involved question must TRAVERSE participants,
#   and gives the lookup-and-resolve filter for doing it. The prompt also gains the two-status
#   document rule: currency is clinical:documentReferenceStatus (current | superseded |
#   entered-in-error) and NOT clinical:status (the composition status), whose "amended" means
#   corrected content on a document that is usually still current. Newly answerable and taught
#   with them: clinical:encounterReason, clinical:admitSource (its presence is the only signal
#   an encounter was an admission), clinical:dischargeDisposition, clinical:encounterClassDisplay
#   (+ClassSystem, because the class binding is extensible so a bare code may be local),
#   coverage:status (a cancelled plan read as active is a wrong answer to "am I covered"), and
#   clinical:documentAuthorName 0..* vs clinical:authenticatorName (wrote it vs signed it).
#   clinical:businessIdentifier (FHIR token form system|value, cross-transport comparable) is
#   taught as NOT interchangeable with clinical:sourceRecordId (a server-assigned logical id);
#   the two id spaces do not join. core 3.7 adds cascade:hasAttachment -> cascade:Attachment
#   (path / mediaType / contentHash+hashAlgorithm), bytes as a pod-relative FILE, not a literal.
#   health 2.8 carries no agent-facing change and is recorded to keep the rows in step.
# ALSO FIXED HERE, and not a vocabulary change: every core-vocabulary property comes back
#   from `cascade pod query --json` prefixed core:, never cascade:, because cascade-cli binds
#   both prefixes to one namespace and resolves core: first. Every filter in the prompt that
#   read .properties["cascade:*"] was returning null against a real pod and reporting it as
#   absent data. Filters now read core: first with a cascade: fallback. The prompt also now
#   teaches the two other flattening losses in that JSON: repeatable properties are joined
#   into ONE ", "-delimited string (safe to split only for IRIs and codes, never free text),
#   and structural sub-nodes share their owner's bucket and are counted in its `count`, so
#   an --encounters count is visits PLUS participants.
core=3.7
health=2.8
clinical=1.16
coverage=1.5
checkup=3.3
pots=1.4
